1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,460
A ceiling fan hangs in Diya's room.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,216
How would you tell a
friend exactly where it is?

3
00:00:05,616 --> 00:00:10,031
Two numbers can find a spot on the
floor: so far from one wall, so far

4
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,137
from the other.

5
00:00:11,137 --> 00:00:13,180
But the fan is up in the air.

6
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:15,900
Diya wondered about this
in her room tonight.

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,215
Floor numbers are not enough.

8
00:00:18,215 --> 00:00:19,630
So what is missing?

9
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:22,071
A third number: how high.

10
00:00:22,071 --> 00:00:24,575
Welcome to three dimensional geometry.

11
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:27,234
Start at one corner of the room.

12
00:00:27,234 --> 00:00:30,923
Three edges meet there, each at
right angles to the other two.

13
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:33,725
Turn the edges into number lines.

14
00:00:33,725 --> 00:00:39,009
The x axis runs along one wall, the y
axis along the other, and the z axis

15
00:00:39,009 --> 00:00:40,369
goes straight up.

16
00:00:40,769 --> 00:00:43,910
The corner where they
meet is the origin, O.

17
00:00:44,310 --> 00:00:48,498
Each pair of axes makes a flat
sheet, called a coordinate plane.

18
00:00:48,498 --> 00:00:50,479
The floor is the XY plane.

19
00:00:50,479 --> 00:00:53,940
The two walls are the YZ
plane and the ZX plane.

20
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:55,926
Now find the fan.

21
00:00:55,926 --> 00:00:57,411
Start at the origin.

22
00:00:57,811 --> 00:01:01,309
Walk three steps along x,
then four steps along y.

23
00:01:01,309 --> 00:01:03,611
You are now right under the fan.

24
00:01:04,011 --> 00:01:07,450
Now climb two steps up
z, and you reach the fan.

25
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,727
So the fan is at the
point three, four, two.

26
00:01:11,327 --> 00:01:13,009
NCERT puts it like this.

27
00:01:13,009 --> 00:01:16,345
x is the distance of the
point from the YZ plane.

28
00:01:16,345 --> 00:01:18,883
y is its distance from the ZX plane.

29
00:01:18,883 --> 00:01:21,671
And z is its distance from the XY plane.

30
00:01:22,421 --> 00:01:23,568
Side by side.

31
00:01:23,568 --> 00:01:26,636
On an axis, two of the numbers are zero.

32
00:01:26,636 --> 00:01:30,308
A point on the x axis
looks like x, zero, zero.

33
00:01:30,708 --> 00:01:33,529
On a plane, only one number is zero.

34
00:01:33,529 --> 00:01:38,183
Every point on the floor, the
XY plane, has z equal to zero.

35
00:01:38,183 --> 00:01:40,992
And the origin is zero, zero, zero.

36
00:01:41,592 --> 00:01:42,492
Your turn.

37
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:45,166
Where is the point zero, five, three?

38
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:47,854
On the YZ plane, or on the y axis?

39
00:01:47,854 --> 00:01:49,129
Pause and decide.

40
00:01:52,329 --> 00:01:53,809
On the YZ plane!

41
00:01:53,809 --> 00:01:55,119
Only x is zero.

42
00:01:55,119 --> 00:01:59,010
For the y axis, x and z
would both have to be zero.

43
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:00,638
Remember this.

44
00:02:00,638 --> 00:02:05,485
Every point in space needs three numbers,
x, y and z, one for each direction.

45
00:02:06,185 --> 00:02:11,083
The axes also run backwards, past
the origin, into negative numbers.

46
00:02:11,483 --> 00:02:15,403
So the three planes cut all of space
into eight parts, called octants.

47
00:02:15,803 --> 00:02:18,100
The signs tell you which octant.

48
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:21,800
In the first octant, x,
y and z are all positive.

49
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:27,132
Make z negative, and the point drops
below the floor, into the fifth octant.

50
00:02:27,532 --> 00:02:30,829
Make all three negative, and
you are in the seventh octant.

51
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:33,169
Now, one worked example.

52
00:02:33,519 --> 00:02:36,502
Take the point P, three, minus four, five.

53
00:02:36,502 --> 00:02:40,922
Name its octant, find its distance
from each plane, and its foot on the

54
00:02:40,922 --> 00:02:41,822
floor.

55
00:02:42,003 --> 00:02:42,903
Step one.

56
00:02:42,765 --> 00:02:45,004
The signs are plus, minus, plus.

57
00:02:45,004 --> 00:02:46,722
That is the fourth octant.

58
00:02:47,472 --> 00:02:48,372
Step two.

59
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,988
Distance from the YZ plane is three.

60
00:02:50,988 --> 00:02:53,015
From the ZX plane, four.

61
00:02:53,015 --> 00:02:55,042
From the XY plane, five.

62
00:02:55,792 --> 00:02:56,713
Step three.

63
00:02:56,713 --> 00:02:59,245
Drop straight down to the XY plane.

64
00:02:59,245 --> 00:03:01,577
Keep x and y, and make z zero.

65
00:03:01,577 --> 00:03:04,249
The foot is three, minus four, zero.

66
00:03:04,999 --> 00:03:08,264
So one point gives you three
distances and a shadow on the floor.

67
00:03:08,914 --> 00:03:10,376
Now, the exam trap.

68
00:03:10,726 --> 00:03:14,967
For the point minus three, two, five,
many students say its distance from

69
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:16,848
the YZ plane is minus three.

70
00:03:17,248 --> 00:03:19,328
But a distance is never negative.

71
00:03:19,328 --> 00:03:20,275
It is three.

72
00:03:20,275 --> 00:03:24,553
The minus sign only tells you which
side of the plane the point is on.

73
00:03:25,203 --> 00:03:26,708
Where is this asked?

74
00:03:26,708 --> 00:03:31,394
We found no past paper question on
just this idea, so no chip lights.

75
00:03:31,394 --> 00:03:35,989
The type: name the octant, or
find a foot on an axis or a plane.

76
00:03:36,589 --> 00:03:37,750
Exam level now.

77
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:41,303
A point P, a, b, c, lies
in the fourth octant.

78
00:03:41,303 --> 00:03:46,195
Its distances from the XY, YZ and
ZX planes are six, two and three.

79
00:03:46,195 --> 00:03:47,829
Find a plus b plus c.

80
00:03:47,829 --> 00:03:49,040
Pause and solve.

81
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,034
The answer is B.

82
00:03:56,034 --> 00:03:56,934
Five.

83
00:03:57,227 --> 00:04:01,876
Distance from the YZ plane is
the size of x, so a is two.

84
00:04:01,876 --> 00:04:06,524
Distance from the XY plane is
the size of z, so c is six.

85
00:04:07,024 --> 00:04:11,350
Distance from the ZX plane is
the size of y, which is three.

86
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:15,451
In the fourth octant, y is
negative, so b is minus three.

87
00:04:15,951 --> 00:04:18,479
Two, minus three and six add up to five.

88
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:20,619
Here is your recap.

89
00:04:20,619 --> 00:04:22,201
Screenshot this card.

90
00:04:25,401 --> 00:04:27,587
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

91
00:04:27,987 --> 00:04:28,887
One.

92
00:04:28,432 --> 00:04:31,629
Which number is zero for
every point on the ZX plane?

93
00:04:32,529 --> 00:04:33,429
Two.

94
00:04:33,026 --> 00:04:36,777
Which octant holds the point
minus two, five, minus one?

95
00:04:37,677 --> 00:04:38,577
Three.

96
00:04:38,241 --> 00:04:42,686
What is the foot of the point four,
minus one, six on the XY plane?

97
00:04:43,786 --> 00:04:47,238
Next time: a stick fits
corner to corner inside a box.

98
00:04:47,238 --> 00:04:48,392
How long is it?

99
00:04:48,392 --> 00:04:50,867
The distance formula in three dimensions.
